     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Linking and changes",
     "texto": [
      "When a syllable ends in a consonant and the next one starts with a placeholder ㅇ, the consonant usually links to the vowel: 한국어 is divided 한-국-어 and 옷이 links as 옷-이. The result cannot always be worked out by looking at just one isolated consonant.",
      "In 감사합니다, ㅂ before ㄴ becomes nasalised and is heard as m. There are more sound changes; you will learn them through patterns and common words."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
